The flip grace (linux-drm-virtio-flip-grace) completes a flip committed up to
flip_grace_us after the host's tick for that tick.  It did so even when the
tick already had its flip: a flip whose event went out at the tick, and a
second one in its grace, were both for that tick.  The compositor, told its
frame was on the screen, drew the next at once, and the host showed one of
the two at that blank and nothing new at the next - a GNOME guest whose
flips fell near the grace's edge ran at half rate for seconds at a time
(the research's gdl13, gdl17/18, 2026-11-08: its frames 2.0 then 6.3 ms
apart; 46 % of its flips in the grace in those seconds, 6 % otherwise; no
such spell in 3 boots with flip_grace_us=0, in 6 of 7 with 1200).

The grace now holds only for a tick that has no flip yet: each output keeps
the vblank its last flip event went out for, or is due at, and a second
flip in the grace waits for the next tick (module parameter
flip_grace_once, default 1; 0 = the grace for any flip in it, as before).
debugfs virtio-gpu-flip-gate counts the flips completed in a grace and the
second flips in the grace of a tick that had one, in both modes.

